## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-pattern | Why it fails |
| ------------ | ------------ |
| "Big bang" task touching many layers | Un-reviewable, un-revertable |
| Task with no failing test first | No proof the change was needed |
| Acceptance criteria written after coding | Confirmation bias, scope drift |
| Hidden dependency between "independent" tasks | Breaks the main branch on partial merge |
